hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"31","Al-Barā' reported: A man was reciting Sūrat Al-Kahf and his horse was tied with two ropes beside him. A cloud came down and spread over that man, and it kept on coming closer and closer to him till his horse started jumping (as if afraid of something). When it was morning, the man came to the Prophet, and told him of that experience. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \That was tranquility which descended because of (the recitation of) the Qur'an.\"" Reference: Sahih al-Bukhari 5011"""""
"32","Abu al-Dardā’ reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ﷺ said: “Whoever memorizes the first ten verses from Sūrat al-Kahf (The Cave) will be protected from the Dajjāl.” Reference: Sahih Muslim 809"
"33","Abu Dāwūd mentioned that it was reported with a variation through Qatādah, “…whoever memorizes the concluding verses of Sūrat al-Kahf,” and from Shu’bah via Qatādah, “from the end of Al-Kahf…” Reference: Sunan ad-Darimi 4323"
